S entry update), then restarted the node to prove persistence — post-reboot /proc/cmdline confirms audit=1 is active and the boot_id changed, proving a real restart occurred.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Captured baseline: /proc/cmdline had no audit param, boot_id=f43afa1c-4877-4ace-a101-d6bb0cd6ce3d\",\"Ran `sudo grubby --update-kernel=ALL --args=\\\"audit=1\\\"` on node1 to persist the kernel parameter into the BLS boot entry\",\"Verified the BLS entry (/boot/loader/entries/*.conf) and grubby --info=ALL now show audit=1 in args\",\"Issued `sudo systemctl reboot` in background so the ack returned before disconnection\",\"Polled node1 until exec succeeded again\",\"Verified new boot_id=b873bcc9-2e73-480e-a49b-00835cb76918 (changed from baseline) and new uptime -s, proving an actual restart\",\"Verified post-reboot /proc/cmdline contains audit=1, proving the setting persisted across the reboot\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Baseline kernel cmdline had no audit=1 before change\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2f88678db9834ab7\",\"cmd-723d4d17ade54ed8\"],\"summary\":\"/proc/cmdline and grubby --info=ALL show no audit parameter; boot_id captured as f43afa1c-4877-4ace-a101-d6bb0cd6ce3d\"},{\"requirement\":\"audit=1 persisted into bootloader (BLS entry) via grubby\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-476c0789463e4879\",\"cmd-60327509478546e4\"],\"summary\":\"grubby --update-kernel=ALL --args=\\\"audit=1\\\" applied; grubby --info=ALL and /boot/loader/entries/*.conf both show audit=1 in args before reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1c82eaa3ea294459\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl reboot issued in background, command returned pid immediately\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node restart proven via changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7c6c4e9537f6465d\",\"cmd-905ed89e2c804d2f\"],\"summary\":\"Connection timed out while node was down, then exec succeeded again with boot_id b873bcc9-2e73-480e-a49b-00835cb76918 (different from baseline f43afa1c...) and new uptime -s timestamp\"},{\"requirement\":\"audit=1 kernel parameter active and persistent after reboot\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-781d9480f6874f38\"],\"summary\":\"Post-reboot /proc/cmdline shows audit=1 present in the live running kernel command line, confirming the grubby change survived the restart\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1's kernel to boot with audit=1 persistently via grubby (BLS entry update), then restarted the node to prove persistence — post-reboot /proc/cmdline confirms audit=1 is active and the boot_id changed, proving a real restart occurred.","actions_performed":["Captured baseline: /proc/cmdline had no audit param, boot_id=f43afa1c-4877-4ace-a101-d6bb0cd6ce3d","Ran `sudo grubby --update-kernel=ALL --args=\"audit=1\"` on node1 to persist the kernel parameter into the BLS boot entry","Verified the BLS entry (/boot/loader/entries/*.conf) and grubby --info=ALL now show audit=1 in args","Issued `sudo systemctl reboot` in background so the ack returned before disconnection","Polled node1 until exec succeeded again","Verified new boot_id=b873bcc9-2e73-480e-a49b-00835cb76918 (changed from baseline) and new uptime -s, proving an actual restart","Verified post-reboot /proc/cmdline contains audit=1, proving the setting persisted across the reboot"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Baseline kernel cmdline had no audit=1 before change","command_ids":["cmd-2f88678db9834ab7","cmd-723d4d17ade54ed8"],"summary":"/proc/cmdline and grubby --info=ALL show no audit parameter; boot_id captured as f43afa1c-4877-4ace-a101-d6bb0cd6ce3d"},{"requirement":"audit=1 persisted into bootloader (BLS entry) via grubby","command_ids":["cmd-476c0789463e4879","cmd-60327509478546e4"],"summary":"grubby --update-kernel=ALL --args=\"audit=1\" applied; grubby --info=ALL and /boot/loader/entries/*.conf both show audit=1 in args before reboot"},{"requirement":"Node restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect","comman